# gow-native-pc: launcher-side effect switches. Apply from the workspace root with git apply; this is not a
# runtime-clone patch (the clone carries Tobiichi's own launcher, with different Main.qml/lanzador.cpp).
#
# v2 (2026-11-06), dead-toggle fix: the first version added the three Settings properties, the Graphics page
# group and bandera("GOW_FX_*") in lanzador.cpp, but Main.qml's jugar() play map did not contain the three
# keys. Lanzador::iniciar reads a.value("fxSin*") from that map, so every toggle read as false and the three
# environment variables were always removed: no switch could ever change anything. The follow-up hunks at the
# end of this file forward the keys, include them in the session-diagnostics allowlist and add an assertion to
# tools/test/regional-play-ui.py (plus the mod-model stub that test needed to run at all).
# Verified: regional-play-ui.py passes with Qt 6.8.3 / qml.exe, every a.value key is present in the play map.
#
# v3 (2026-11-06), evidence fix: gow-session.exe records the runtime environment in the session report,
# but its allowlist omitted the three GOW_FX_* variables and the picture settings, so a report could not
# prove whether a switch reached the runner. The last hunk adds them. Also changed outside this patch
# (workspace sources/docs, no runtime clone involved): play-asia.cmd (no blind overrides + settings note),
# tools/test/launcher-env-contract.py (new contract test), tools/pipeline/modules/verify.ps1 (runs it),
# engine/README.md (patch 81 moved out of the runtime chain).
#
